"\nTARGET 4 docs/reviews/README.md prose\u002dentrypoint\nIDENTITY e0d2de71d89ffbdf49ee8d9f6b7b7e902a8858f0 62db9a24c864113f64c8fb97913f5364cc64f11f243a70f352fe93a577c1195e RANGES [[1, 166]] MASKED [12]\n1: # Reviews: the codebase renovation program (M6)\n2: \n3: The whole codebase, reviewed and brought up to date in slices, progressively,\n4: beside feature work (D\u002dWORKFLOW\u002d083, D\u002dWORKFLOW\u002d102, D\u002dWORKFLOW\u002d181), and it gates no release (D\u002dWORKFLOW\u002d187). The\n5: milestone is M6; the epic is #339; the plan for the plan is #346.\n6: \n7: | File | What it is | Written by |\n8: | \u002d\u002d\u002d | \u002d\u002d\u002d | \u002d\u002d\u002d |\n9: | `plan\u002dfor\u002dthe\u002dplan.md` | how the program is planned: the survey, the slicing, the ordering lenses, the per\u002dslice procedure, the brief an executor receives, the drift rules, the ledgers | P0 (#346) |\n10: | `order.md` | the slices in order, each with its lens, paths, line count, any reading\u002dorder prerequisite (the renovation gates no release, D\u002dWORKFLOW\u002d187), its depth and the evidence that closes it (#346's first criterion) | P1 |\n11: | `inventory.json`, `inventory.md` | every path's root, provenance tier, language, lines, patches, last fork and upstream commits, reachability; the per\u002darea totals | `tools/renovation\u002dinventory` (P1), re\u002drun at every slice close |\n12: [MASKED sensitive\u002dlabelled line; not read unredacted]\n13: | `cross\u002dreference.md` | every area against every other: call edges, shared state, rule\u002dto\u002darea and patch\u002dto\u002darea edges | `tools/renovation\u002dinventory \u002d\u002dcross` (P1) |\n14: | `slices.json` | the order's hand\u002dwritten input: each slice's number, area, kind, lens, selector, reading\u002dorder prerequisite (`read_before`), depth, interacting subsystems and closing evidence; the security, state and launch\u002dpath globs the drift tool reads | P1, then the planner when the order changes |\n15: | `areas.json` | the area map: every tracked path in exactly one area (the one hand\u002dwritten input to the inventory) | P1, edited when an area is split or an epic filed |\n16: | `p1\u002dtracking.md` | the survey's multi\u002dpass tracking file: hashes, counts with their commands, each pass's evidence | P1 |\n17: | `status.md` | the `order:` row, then one row per slice: area, lines, depth, state, issue, reviewed\u002dat, fixed\u002dat, drift since | `tools/renovation\u002dstatus \u002d\u002dwrite docs/reviews/status.md` (P1), at every slice close |\n18: | `drift.md` | per closed slice, what changed under its paths since `fixed\u002dat` | `tools/renovation\u002ddrift \u002d\u002dwrite docs/reviews/drift.md`, at every slice close, the renovation's own cadence, not a release step (D\u002dWORKFLOW\u002d187) |\n19: | `briefs/<slice>.md` | the brief an executing session runs a slice from, ten sections, committed before dispatch | the planner |\n20: \n21: The audits themselves live under `docs/audits/<date>\u002depic\u002dm6\u002d<slice>/`, the\n22: retros under `docs/retros/`, and the decisions in `docs/decision\u002dregister.md`.\n23: \n24: ## The tools\n25: \n26: All fork\u002donly (listed in `fork\u002dworkflow.md` \u00a7 Personal paths, `PERSONAL_PATTERNS`\n27: in `.githooks/pre\u002dpush`, and `instruction\u002dfiles.md` \u00a7 The fork's own tools).\n28: \n29: ### `tools/renovation\u002dinventory`\n30: \n31: Writes `inventory.json` (a header, the column names, then one row per tracked\n32: path of both trees, sorted) and `inventory.md` (the per\u002darea totals and the\n33: unreached and unshipped sets). The hand\u002dwritten input is `areas.json`: a list\n34: of `{\"area\", \"epic\", \"globs\"}`, where a glob is relative to the distribution\n35: unless prefixed `es:`, a `!` glob excludes within its own area, `**` crosses\n36: `/`, and `{a,b}` alternates globs (no nesting).\n37: \n38: It prints five lines and exits 1 unless each pair agrees and both counters are\n39: 0, or 2 when it cannot run:\n40: \n41: ```\n42: paths: N (git ls\u002dfiles: N)        # the distribution at HEAD\n43: es\u002dpaths: N (git ls\u002dfiles: N)     # the ES checkout at HEAD (a detached worktree at the pin)\n44: patches: N (find: N)              # *.patch under packages/ and projects/\n45: unassigned: N                     # a path in no area\n46: ambiguous: N                      # a path in two or more areas\n47: ```\n48: \n49: What its columns mean:\n50: \n51: \u002d **tier**: `fork\u002down` (changed since the merge base with `upstream/next`, or\n52:   on ES with `rocknix/master`), `upstream\u002dcarried` (everything else), or\n53:   `vendor\u002dcarried` (every `*.patch` and kernel `linux*.conf` under\n54:   `packages/` or `projects/`, with `tier_note: fork\u002dwritten` when fork\u002down).\n55:   `overlap` marks a fork\u002down path upstream also changed since the base.\n56: \u002d **lines**: git's numstat against the empty tree; `null` for a binary.\n57: \u002d **patches**: on a `package.mk` row, the patches under that package's own\n58:   directory; `null` elsewhere.\n59: \u002d **last_fork_commit**, **last_upstream_commit**: `<hash10> <date>` of the\n60:   newest commit touching the path on each side, from one `git log\n61:   \u002d\u002dname\u002donly` pass per side.\n62: \u002d **reach**: `shipped` (in a plan of a device we ship: H700 and SM8550,\n63:   D\u002dWORKFLOW\u002d185), `test` (in the test image's plan, GENERIC_X64, and no\n64:   shipped device's), `unshipped` (only in other devices' plans), `unreached` (a\n65:   package or project path no plan reaches), `n/a` (a path no image plan can\n66:   hold: the build engine, tools, doctrine, records). `reachable_by` and\n67:   `buildable_by` name the plans.\n68: \n69: How reachability is computed. `tools/viewplan` runs once per device and\n70: architecture the `Makefile` builds (`image` for 64\u002dbit, the virtual `arm` for\n71: 32\u002dbit where `ENABLE_32BIT` is true), in the **build image the Makefile pins by\n72: digest**, with the checkout mounted read\u002donly and no network. It does not run\n73: on the host by default: the host lacks `xmlstarlet`, which\n74: `distributions/ROCKNIX/config/functions` uses to compute `SUBDEVICES` with its\n75: errors discarded, so a host plan silently drops H700's and RK3566's subdevice\n76: bootloaders (`\u002d\u002drunner host` is the explicit, recorded alternative). Each\n77: plan package is then sourced with `source_package`, and its `PKG_DIR`,\n78: `PKG_VERSION`, `PATCH_ARCH` and `PKG_PATCH_DIRS` give exactly the patch\n79: directories `scripts/unpack` would apply. A path in a package directory is\n80: reached when that directory is a plan package's `PKG_DIR` (a patch only when\n81: its directory is selected); a generic `package.mk` sourced by a reached\n82: override is reached with it; a device's own files by that device's plans;\n83: `projects/ROCKNIX`'s bootloader, filesystem, options and `config.xml` by\n84: every plan; the other projects and the other `distributions/` (nothing sets\n85: `DISTRO` but its `ROCKNIX` default) by none; the ES tree by the plans that build\n86: `emulationstation`. Reachability errs toward reached: a file in a reached\n87: package counts as reached even when its recipe installs it only for some\n88: devices, so `unreached` is a conservative claim and the slice read refines\n89: the rest.\n90: \n91: `\u002d\u002dassess` writes `assessment.md` from the committed `inventory.json` and the\n92: tracker (`gh issue list \u002d\u002drepo pixelelated/distribution`, bounded, failing if\n93: a list reaches its limit): per area, over its reached code files, the files\n94: matching the brief's security tokens; the blindspot entries, friction lines,\n95: closed bugs and open issues naming one of the area's identifiers (its units'\n96: and code files' names, six characters or more) as a whole word; commits since\n97: 2026\u002d06\u002d01 and the change since the merge base on both trees; callers of its\n98: ten largest units outside it; its unreached and unshipped sizes. Every count\n99: is a search, so a lead: the slice read confirms or overturns it. Records are\n100: not scored.\n101: \n102: `\u002d\u002dcross` writes `cross\u002dreference.md`: for every ordered pair of the ten code\n103: areas, the area's code files naming an identifier only the other area owns;\n104: the shared state (`system.cfg`, `es_settings.cfg`, the cloud configuration,\n105: stamps and lock, `rclone.conf`, `retroarch.cfg`, the proxy's state, ...)\n106: each area touches; each rule's `paths:` globs resolved to areas; each patch\n107: against the area of the package it patches.\n108: \n109: `\u002d\u002dorder` reads `slices.json`, puts every inventory row in its slice (a row\n110: belongs to a slice when its area is one of the slice's, it matches the\n111: slice's globs, and its reach is one the slice names; a `rest` slice takes\n112: only rows no other slice in its area claims), prints each slice's paths,\n113: lines, read lines and fork\u002down read lines, and renders the block of\n114: `order.md` between its markers. It exits 1 when a row is in no slice or in\n115: two, when a slice is empty, or when one of the first three reads more than\n116: 12,000 lines (a currency slice counts its fork\u002down lines, a table none).\n117: `\u002d\u002dno\u002dwrite` prints only.\n118: \n119: `\u002d\u002dslice\u002dissues DIR` writes each slice issue's title (`M6.P2 E339/T<k>: <area>:\n120: <title>`) and body (scope, `reviewed\u002dat:` and `fixed\u002dat:` empty, the VM\n121: question, five agent\u002dverifiable criteria) into DIR, from `slices.json` and\n122: `inventory.json`; it touches no tracker. Pass 7 files them after the\n123: maintainer's yes.\n124: \n125: `\u002d\u002dself\u002dtest` proves the area counters and the glob rules can fail;\n126: `\u002d\u002dinject\u002dpath PATH` adds a synthetic path to a real run (it must fail with\n127: `unassigned: 1`); `\u002d\u002dplans DIR` keeps the plan files.\n128: \n129: ### `tools/renovation\u002ddrift`\n130: \n131: For every slice in `slices.json` with a `fixed_at` (a distribution commit,\n132: plus `es` for EmulationStation paths), `git diff \u002d\u002dnumstat <fixed_at>..next`\n133: filtered to the slice's paths (the same membership `\u002d\u002dorder` uses; the ES\n134: target is the pin `next` carries). It reports files, lines changed, the share\n135: of the slice's lines, and any `sensitive` file touched, with plan \u00a7 8's\n136: verdict: `small` (under 20 % and nothing sensitive: an issue\u002dtier pass over\n137: the diff) or `re\u002dopen`. Exit 1 when any slice must re\u002dopen, 2 when it cannot\n138: run. `\u002d\u002dpretend SLICE=HASH[,es=HASH]` sets a `fixed_at` for one run: on\n139: 2026\u002d10\u002d22 a pretend close of T1 at the merge base reported `re\u002dopen`\n140: (29 files, 3,273 lines, 24.6 %, all three sensitive lists) and exit 1, and\n141: the same at `HEAD` reported `none` and exit 0. `\u002d\u002dself\u002dtest` checks the\n142: thresholds.\n143: \n144: ### `tools/renovation\u002dstatus`\n145: \n146: Writes `status.md`: the `order:` row from `order.md`'s review status line,\n147: then one row per slice, its lines from the inventory, its depth from\n148: `slices.json`, and its state from the slice issue on milestone M6 (title\n149: `M6.P2 E<epic>/T<k>: ...`; body lines `reviewed\u002dat:`, `fixed\u002dat:`,\n150: `fixed\u002dat\u002des:`) and the audit folders: `unreviewed`, `reading`,\n151: `remediating`, `closed`, or `drifted` (closed, and `renovation\u002ddrift` says\n152: re\u002dopen). One bounded `gh issue list`; it fails at its limit.\n153: \n154: ### The renovation face of `tools/lint\u002daudit\u002dartifacts`\n155: \n156: For an audit folder whose name carries `\u002depic\u002dm6\u002d` (a renovation slice), the\n157: lint also requires a `## Renovation face` section in `04\u002danalysis.md` with a\n158: `### Q1` to `### Q7` subsection each (plan \u00a7 4's seven questions), a\n159: `punch_index` YAML block, and on every item `question: Q1..Q7`, or\n160: `question: none` with its reason on the line or in `question_reason:`.\n161: `tools/test\u002dfixtures/lint\u002daudit\u002dartifacts/fixture\u002depic\u002dm6\u002drenovation\u002dpass`\n162: passes (`PASS`, rc 0) and `...\u002dfail`, the same folder without the face,\n163: fails on exactly those two checks (rc 1). On 2026\u002d10\u002d22 a face missing Q4\n164: and a `question: none` without a reason each failed alone, and the 21\n165: existing audit folders kept their verdicts.\n\nTARGET 9 .github/sessions/saved\u002dsession\u002dstate\u002dfeature\u002dm6\u002drenovation\u002dplan\u002d346.md prose\u002dentrypoint\nIDENTITY cecbab950fdc6a8293df3b40610e4e6ce3631f78 d5e8c9fa4b631cee2910d409aac058a4d1aebc9c87df22243f109ed87ddb2306 RANGES [[1, 49]] MASKED [46]\n1: # M6 coordinator current handoff\n2: \n3: Updated 2026\u002d11\u002d03T00:49:06.287070+00:00 by Codex / GPT\u002d6\u002dAstra / xhigh (own observed footer, not provider\u002dattested), session01a19d11\u002df5c8\u002d7bb0\u002d80f3\u002d49ad28732af2, wN:p2.\n4: \n5: ## Resume here\n6: \n7: Worktree `/workspace/repos/pixelelated/distribution.worktrees/m6\u002drenovation\u002dplan\u002d346`, branch `feature/m6\u002drenovation\u002dplan\u002d346`. User authorizes continued M6 work in existing wN lanes, normal scoped commits/pushes and tracker coordination. Milestone6 body is the current ordered queue. Read current rules and plan \u00a76b/\u00a77/\u00a78 before dispatch. Older detailed continuity is preserved at `8b83e452459f6696ac959b4e4e5494701d5d2f93` in this same path; its pending\u002dstate prose is historical.\n8: \n9: ## Current lanes and acceptance boundaries\n10: \n11: Updated 2026\u002d11\u002d02T23:46:39.152621+00:00. T39/T41/T42 accepted/completion verified; actual ordered area integration remains pending.\n12: \n13: | Lane | Current outcome | Next useful action |\n14: 